, language and tier, all in one view."}, {"id": "D8", "text": "A profit curve: rupees gained for every call list size from 0 to the whole population, using your offer cost and success rate, with your capacity marked."}, {"id": "D11", "text": "Voluntary against involuntary churn by month and payment method."}, {"id": "D13", "text": "A segment page for Monthly subscribers."}]}, {"key": "documentation", "title": "Phase 4, Documentation", "tasks": [{"id": "DOC1", "text": "Write a model card plus a business memo. The model card covers data, population, label, leakage you removed, features, validation and test results. The memo, for the head of growth, says how many people to call, who, and what it is worth in rupees with an offer of ₹129 saving 40% of churners, and what to do about involuntary churn, which a phone call will not fix."}]}, {"key": "stretch", "title": "Stretch ideas (optional)", "tasks": [{"id": "X-S6", "text": "Check your model for fairness across tiers and languages: precision and recall by group."}, {"id": "X-S3", "text": "Is the FIRST99 promo worth it? Compare 12 month revenue per subscriber with and without it."}, {"id": "X-S2", "text": "Estimate how much revenue would be saved by retrying failed renewals on day 1, 3 and 7 instead of only day 3."}]}], "brief": "**Your business brief (shared with 4 other buyers):** segment **Monthly subscribers**, offer cost **₹129**, save rate **40%**, call capacity **1000**."}$pack$::jsonb
