D6", "text": "Model page header: AUC, PR AUC, base rate and the lift in the top 10% on the test window."}, {"id": "D11", "text": "Voluntary against involuntary churn by month and payment method."}, {"id": "D15", "text": "Make every panel respect the segment filters."}, {"id": "D9", "text": "Churn rate by cycle, plan, payment method, language and tier, all in one view."}]}, {"key": "documentation", "title": "Phase 4, Documentation", "tasks": [{"id": "DOC1", "text": "Write a model card plus a business memo. The model card covers data, population, label, leakage you removed, features, validation and test results. The memo, for the head of growth, says how many people to call, who, and what it is worth in rupees with an offer of ₹49 saving 25% of churners, and what to do about involuntary churn, which a phone call will not fix."}]}, {"key": "stretch", "title": "Stretch ideas (optional)", "tasks": [{"id": "X-S4", "text": "Survival analysis: Kaplan-Meier curves by billing cycle and channel."}, {"id": "X-S1", "text": "Build a separate model for involuntary churn using only payment history, and compare it with the main model on those churners."}, {"id": "X-S3", "text": "Is the FIRST99 promo worth it? Compare 12 month revenue per subscriber with and without it."}]}], "brief": "**Your business brief (shared with 4 other buyers):** segment **Net Banking payers**, offer cost **₹49**, save rate **25%**, call capacity **1200**."}$pack$::jsonb
