"text": "A profit curve: rupees gained for every call list size from 0 to the whole population, using your offer cost and success rate, with your capacity marked."}, {"id": "D6", "text": "Model page header: AUC, PR AUC, base rate and the lift in the top 10% on the test window."}, {"id": "D9", "text": "Churn rate by cycle, plan, payment method, language and tier, all in one view."}]}, {"key": "documentation", "title": "Phase 4, Documentation", "tasks": [{"id": "DOC1", "text": "Write a model card plus a business memo. The model card covers data, population, label, leakage you removed, features, validation and test results. The memo, for the head of growth, says how many people to call, who, and what it is worth in rupees with an offer of ₹129 saving 40% of churners, and what to do about involuntary churn, which a phone call will not fix."}]}, {"key": "stretch", "title": "Stretch ideas (optional)", "tasks": [{"id": "X-S6", "text": "Check your model for fairness across tiers and languages: precision and recall by group."}, {"id": "X-S5", "text": "Which features would you add if you could log one more thing in the app? Justify with the data."}, {"id": "X-S2", "text": "Estimate how much revenue would be saved by retrying failed renewals on day 1, 3 and 7 instead of only day 3."}]}], "brief": "**Your business brief (shared with 4 other buyers):** segment **FIRST99 promo subscribers**, offer cost **₹129**, save rate **40%**, call capacity **600**.", "premium": [{"id": "X1", "text": "**Uplift, not churn.** Explain why the best people to call are not the highest risk ones, and propose how you would run a test to learn who responds to the offer."}, {"id": "X4", "text": "**Calibrate it.** Calibrate the scores (isotonic or Platt), show the before and after, and explain why the profit calculation needs calibrated probabilities."}, {"id": "X3", "text": "**Optimise the call list.** With your offer cost, success rate and capacity, choose the list that maximises expected rupees, and show the rupee difference against simply calling the top 600 by score."}, {"id": "X5", "text": "**Ship it.** Write the scoring job as a function that takes any cutoff date and returns the call list, with tests that fail if a leaky column ever sneaks back in."}, {"id": "X2", "text": "**Time-based validation done properly.** Add a third, earlier window (cutoff 1 July 2025) and show how stable AUC and feature importance are across the three."}]}$pack$::jsonb
