page header: AUC, PR AUC, base rate and the lift in the top 10% on the test window."}, {"id": "D11", "text": "Voluntary against involuntary churn by month and payment method."}, {"id": "D7", "text": "A calibration chart: predicted against actual churn by score decile."}, {"id": "D10", "text": "The fade: average hours in the months before churn against stayers."}]}, {"key": "documentation", "title": "Phase 4, Documentation", "tasks": [{"id": "DOC1", "text": "Write a model card plus a business memo. The model card covers data, population, label, leakage you removed, features, validation and test results. The memo, for the head of growth, says how many people to call, who, and what it is worth in rupees with an offer of ₹79 saving 30% of churners, and what to do about involuntary churn, which a phone call will not fix."}]}, {"key": "stretch", "title": "Stretch ideas (optional)", "tasks": [{"id": "X-S2", "text": "Estimate how much revenue would be saved by retrying failed renewals on day 1, 3 and 7 instead of only day 3."}, {"id": "X-S6", "text": "Check your model for fairness across tiers and languages: precision and recall by group."}, {"id": "X-S1", "text": "Build a separate model for involuntary churn using only payment history, and compare it with the main model on those churners."}]}], "brief": "**Your business brief (shared with 4 other buyers):** segment **Tamil speakers**, offer cost **₹79**, save rate **30%**, call capacity **1500**."}$pack$::jsonb
