t everyone else."}, {"id": "M2", "text": "Try gradient boosting (LightGBM, XGBoost or scikit-learn) and compare it honestly with the baseline on the test window. Keep whichever wins, and show the five features that matter most."}, {"id": "M3", "text": "Train the same model on a random 80/20 split of the test window and compare its AUC with your time-based number. Explain why the time-based number is the one you report, even if the two come out close."}]}, {"key": "dash1", "title": "Phase 3a, Dashboard Page 1: Subscriber and Call List", "tasks": [{"id": "D4", "text": "Add filters for plan, cycle, payment method, language and tier that also drive the call list."}, {"id": "D5", "text": "Mark involuntary risk separately: subscribers whose last renewal failed at least once."}, {"id": "D3", "text": "Add a call list: the 1000 highest scored subscribers in the test window, with monthly revenue and the reason to call."}, {"id": "D2", "text": "Show the top reasons behind that score (SHAP values, or the features with the biggest effect)."}, {"id": "D1", "text": "Build a subscriber lookup: type a Customer_ID and see the profile, the monthly usage line, bills and tickets on one timeline, and the model's churn score at the test cutoff."}]}, {"key": "dash2", "title": "Phase 3b, Dashboard Page 2: Model and Money", "tasks": [{"id": "D13", "text": "A segment page for Mobile plan."}, {"id": "D6", "text": "Model page header: AUC, PR AUC, base rate and the lift in the top 10% on the test window."}, {"id": "D8", "text": "A profit curve: rupees gained for every call list size from 0 to the whole population, using your offer cost and success rate, with your capacity marked."}, {"id": "D12", "text": "Feature importance for the final model, with leaky features shown greyed out as excluded."}, {"id": "D7", "text": "A calibration chart: predicted against actual churn by score decile."}, {"id": "D15", "text": "Make every panel respect the segment filters."}, {"id": "D10", "text": "The fade: average hours in the months before churn against stayers."}, {"id": "D9", "text": "Churn rate by cycle, plan, payment method, language and tier, all in one view."}, {"id": "D11", "text": "Voluntary against involuntary churn by month and payment method."}, {"id": "D14", "text": "A threshold slider that updates precision, recall, calls made and rupees gained."}]}, {"key": "documentation", "title": "Phase 4, Documentation", "tasks": [{"id": "DOC1", "text": "Write a model card plus a business memo. The model card covers data, population, label, leakage you removed, features, validation and test results. The memo, for the head of growth, says how many people to call, who, and what it is worth in rupees with an offer of ₹79 saving 30% of churners, and what to do about involuntary churn, which a phone call will not fix."}]}, {"key": "stretch", "title": "Stretch ideas (optional)", "tasks": [{"id": "X-S4", "text": "Survival analysis: Kaplan-Meier curves by billing cycle and channel."}, {"id": "X-S2", "text": "Estimate how much revenue would be saved by retrying failed renewals on day 1, 3 and 7 instead of only day 3."}, {"id": "X-S5", "text": "Which features would you add if you could log one more thing in the app? Justify with the data."}]}], "brief": "**Your business brief (shared with 4 other buyers):** segment **Mobile plan**, offer cost **₹79**, save rate **30%**, call capacity **1000**."}$pack$::jsonb
