rage hours in the months before churn against stayers."}, {"id": "D9", "text": "Churn rate by cycle, plan, payment method, language and tier, all in one view."}, {"id": "D11", "text": "Voluntary against involuntary churn by month and payment method."}, {"id": "D14", "text": "A threshold slider that updates precision, recall, calls made and rupees gained."}]}, {"key": "documentation", "title": "Phase 4, Documentation", "tasks": [{"id": "DOC1", "text": "Write a model card plus a business memo. The model card covers data, population, label, leakage you removed, features, validation and test results. The memo, for the head of growth, says how many people to call, who, and what it is worth in rupees with an offer of ₹79 saving 30% of churners, and what to do about involuntary churn, which a phone call will not fix."}]}, {"key": "stretch", "title": "Stretch ideas (optional)", "tasks": [{"id": "X-S4", "text": "Survival analysis: Kaplan-Meier curves by billing cycle and channel."}, {"id": "X-S2", "text": "Estimate how much revenue would be saved by retrying failed renewals on day 1, 3 and 7 instead of only day 3."}, {"id": "X-S5", "text": "Which features would you add if you could log one more thing in the app? Justify with the data."}]}], "brief": "**Your business brief (shared with 4 other buyers):** segment **Mobile plan**, offer cost **₹79**, save rate **30%**, call capacity **1000**."}$pack$::jsonb
