overed). What share of churners never chose to leave, and which payment methods cause it?"}, {"id": "M3", "text": "Train the same model on a random 80/20 split of the test window and compare its AUC with your time-based number. Explain why the time-based number is the one you report, even if the two come out close."}, {"id": "S1", "text": "Churn rate by billing cycle, plan and payment method in the test window, with the population count behind each rate."}]}, {"key": "dash1", "title": "Phase 3a, Dashboard Page 1: Subscriber and Call List", "tasks": [{"id": "D2", "text": "Show the top reasons behind that score (SHAP values, or the features with the biggest effect)."}, {"id": "D5", "text": "Mark involuntary risk separately: subscribers whose last renewal failed at least once."}, {"id": "D4", "text": "Add filters for plan, cycle, payment method, language and tier that also drive the call list."}, {"id": "D1", "text": "Build a subscriber lookup: type a Customer_ID and see the profile, the monthly usage line, bills and tickets on one timeline, and the model's churn score at the test cutoff."}, {"id": "D3", "text": "Add a call list: the 600 highest scored subscribers in the test window, with monthly revenue and the reason to call."}]}, {"key": "dash2", "title": "Phase 3b, Dashboard Page 2: Model and Money", "tasks": [{"id": "D10", "text": "The fade: average hours in the months before churn against stayers."}, {"id": "D7", "text": "A calibration chart: predicted against actual churn by score decile."}, {"id": "D14", "text": "A threshold slider that updates precision, recall, calls made and rupees gained."}, {"id": "D13", "text": "A segment page for UPI Autopay payers."}, {"id": "D8", "text": "A profit curve: rupees gained for every call list size from 0 to the whole population, using your offer cost and success rate, with your capacity marked."}, {"id": "D9", "text": "Churn rate by cycle, plan, payment method, language and tier, all in one view."}, {"id": "D11", "text": "Voluntary against involuntary churn by month and payment method."}, {"id": "D12", "text": "Feature importance for the final model, with leaky features shown greyed out as excluded."}, {"id": "D6", "text": "Model page header: AUC, PR AUC, base rate and the lift in the top 10% on the test window."}, {"id": "D15", "text": "Make every panel respect the segment filters."}]}, {"key": "documentation", "title": "Phase 4, Documentation", "tasks": [{"id": "DOC1", "text": "Write a model card plus a business memo. The model card covers data, population, label, leakage you removed, features, validation and test results. The memo, for the head of growth, says how many people to call, who, and what it is worth in rupees with an offer of ₹79 saving 30% of churners, and what to do about involuntary churn, which a phone call will not fix."}]}, {"key": "stretch", "title": "Stretch ideas (optional)", "tasks": [{"id": "X-S6", "text": "Check your model for fairness across tiers and languages: precision and recall by group."}, {"id": "X-S2", "text": "Estimate how much revenue would be saved by retrying failed renewals on day 1, 3 and 7 instead of only day 3."}, {"id": "X-S1", "text": "Build a separate model for involuntary churn using only payment history, and compare it with the main model on those churners."}]}], "brief": "**Your business brief (shared with 4 other buyers):** segment **UPI Autopay payers**, offer cost **₹79**, save rate **30%**, call capacity **600**.", "premium": [{"id": "X1", "text": "**Uplift, not churn.** Explain why the best people to call are not the highest risk ones, and propose how you would run a test to learn who responds to the offer."}, {"id": "X3", "text": "**Optimise the call list.** With your offer cost, success rate and capacity, choose the list that maximises expected rupees, and show the rupee difference against simply calling the top 600 by score."}, {"id": "X2", "text": "**Time-based validation done properly.** Add a third, earlier window (cutoff 1 July 2025) and show how stable AUC and feature importance are across the three."}, {"id": "X5", "text": "**Ship it.** Write the scoring job as a function that takes any cutoff date and returns the call list, with tests that fail if a leaky column ever sneaks back in."}, {"id": "X4", "text": "**Calibrate it.** Calibrate the scores (isotonic or Platt), show the before and after, and explain why the profit calculation needs calibrated probabilities."}]}$pack$::jsonb
