ers."}, {"id": "D13", "text": "A segment page for Referral acquired."}, {"id": "D7", "text": "A calibration chart: predicted against actual churn by score decile."}, {"id": "D11", "text": "Voluntary against involuntary churn by month and payment method."}, {"id": "D12", "text": "Feature importance for the final model, with leaky features shown greyed out as excluded."}]}, {"key": "documentation", "title": "Phase 4, Documentation", "tasks": [{"id": "DOC1", "text": "Write a model card plus a business memo. The model card covers data, population, label, leakage you removed, features, validation and test results. The memo, for the head of growth, says how many people to call, who, and what it is worth in rupees with an offer of ₹129 saving 40% of churners, and what to do about involuntary churn, which a phone call will not fix."}]}, {"key": "stretch", "title": "Stretch ideas (optional)", "tasks": [{"id": "X-S2", "text": "Estimate how much revenue would be saved by retrying failed renewals on day 1, 3 and 7 instead of only day 3."}, {"id": "X-S4", "text": "Survival analysis: Kaplan-Meier curves by billing cycle and channel."}, {"id": "X-S3", "text": "Is the FIRST99 promo worth it? Compare 12 month revenue per subscriber with and without it."}]}], "brief": "**Your business brief (shared with 4 other buyers):** segment **Referral acquired**, offer cost **₹129**, save rate **40%**, call capacity **1500**."}$pack$::jsonb
