ean billing and tickets: status variants, amounts, timestamps, and the seven ticket categories."}]}, {"key": "sql", "title": "Phase 2, SQL and Modelling: Understand and Predict the Churn", "tasks": [{"id": "S5", "text": "Churn rate by language and tier. Which languages lose subscribers fastest, and is it about the catalogue?"}, {"id": "S8", "text": "**Your segment, Referral acquired:** population, churners, churn rate and involuntary share in the test window, and the monthly revenue those churners took with them."}, {"id": "M4", "text": "**Your money:** with the offer at ₹129, a 40% save rate and 1500 calls, how many rupees does calling your top 1500 subscribers earn on the test window, and how does that compare with calling 1500 at random?"}, {"id": "S7", "text": "Using window functions, compute each subscriber's month on month change in watch hours and the number of consecutive declining months before the cutoff."}, {"id": "M1", "text": "Baseline model: logistic regression on your leak-free features, trained on the October window and tested on the January window. Report AUC, PR AUC and the churn rate in the top 10% of scores."}, {"id": "S4", "text": "Usage before churn: average watch hours in each of the 6 months before churn, separately for voluntary and involuntary churners, against subscribers who stayed. When does the fade start, and who does not fade at all?"}, {"id": "S6", "text": "Tickets: churn rate for subscribers with a buffering ticket or a cancel request in the 90 days before the cutoff, against those without."}, {"id": "S1", "text": "Churn rate by billing cycle, plan and payment method in the test window, with the population count behind each rate."}, {"id": "S2", "text": "Split churn into voluntary and involuntary (renewal payment failed twice and was never recovered). What share of churners never chose to leave, and which payment methods cause it?"}, {"id": "S3", "text": "The FIRST99 promo: churn at the first full price renewal for promo subscribers against everyone else."}, {"id": "M2", "text": "Try gradient boosting (LightGBM, XGBoost or scikit-learn) and compare it honestly with the baseline on the test window. Keep whichever wins, and show the five features that matter most."}, {"id": "M3", "text": "Train the same model on a random 80/20 split of the test window and compare its AUC with your time-based number. Explain why the time-based number is the one you report, even if the two come out close."}]}, {"key": "dash1", "title": "Phase 3a, Dashboard Page 1: Subscriber and Call List", "tasks": [{"id": "D3", "text": "Add a call list: the 1500 highest scored subscribers in the test window, with monthly revenue and the reason to call."}, {"id": "D1", "text": "Build a subscriber lookup: type a Customer_ID and see the profile, the monthly usage line, bills and tickets on one timeline, and the model's churn score at the test cutoff."}, {"id": "D4", "text": "Add filters for plan, cycle, payment method, language and tier that also drive the call list."}, {"id": "D2", "text": "Show the top reasons behind that score (SHAP values, or the features with the biggest effect)."}, {"id": "D5", "text": "Mark involuntary risk separately: subscribers whose last renewal failed at least once."}]}, {"key": "dash2", "title": "Phase 3b, Dashboard Page 2: Model and Money", "tasks": [{"id": "D14", "text": "A threshold slider that updates precision, recall, calls made and rupees gained."}, {"id": "D8", "text": "A profit curve: rupees gained for every call list size from 0 to the whole population, using your offer cost and success rate, with your capacity marked."}, {"id": "D6", "text": "Model page header: AUC, PR AUC, base rate and the lift in the top 10% on the test window."}, {"id": "D15", "text": "Make every panel respect the segment filters."}, {"id": "D9", "text": "Churn rate by cycle, plan, payment method, language and tier, all in one view."}, {"id": "D10", "text": "The fade: average hours in the months before churn against stayers."}, {"id": "D13", "text": "A segment page for Referral acquired."}, {"id": "D7", "text": "A calibration chart: predicted against actual churn by score decile."}, {"id": "D11", "text": "Voluntary against involuntary churn by month and payment method."}, {"id": "D12", "text": "Feature importance for the final model, with leaky features shown greyed out as excluded."}]}, {"key": "documentation", "title": "Phase 4, Documentation", "tasks": [{"id": "DOC1", "text": "Write a model card plus a business memo. The model card covers data, population, label, leakage you removed, features, validation and test results. The memo, for the head of growth, says how many people to call, who, and what it is worth in rupees with an offer of ₹129 saving 40% of churners, and what to do about involuntary churn, which a phone call will not fix."}]}, {"key": "stretch", "title": "Stretch ideas (optional)", "tasks": [{"id": "X-S2", "text": "Estimate how much revenue would be saved by retrying failed renewals on day 1, 3 and 7 instead of only day 3."}, {"id": "X-S4", "text": "Survival analysis: Kaplan-Meier curves by billing cycle and channel."}, {"id": "X-S3", "text": "Is the FIRST99 promo worth it? Compare 12 month revenue per subscriber with and without it."}]}], "brief": "**Your business brief (shared with 4 other buyers):** segment **Referral acquired**, offer cost **₹129**, save rate **40%**, call capacity **1500**.", "premium": [{"id": "X1", "text": "**Uplift, not churn.** Explain why the best people to call are not the highest risk ones, and propose how you would run a test to learn who responds to the offer."}, {"id": "X4", "text": "**Calibrate it.** Calibrate the scores (isotonic or Platt), show the before and after, and explain why the profit calculation needs calibrated probabilities."}, {"id": "X2", "text": "**Time-based validation done properly.** Add a third, earlier window (cutoff 1 July 2025) and show how stable AUC and feature importance are across the three."}, {"id": "X5", "text": "**Ship it.** Write the scoring job as a function that takes any cutoff date and returns the call list, with tests that fail if a leaky column ever sneaks back in."}, {"id": "X3", "text": "**Optimise the call list.** With your offer cost, success rate and capacity, choose the list that maximises expected rupees, and show the rupee difference against simply calling the top 1500 by score."}]}$pack$::jsonb
from public.datasets where slug = 'the-quiet-quitters-ott-churn'
on conflict (license_code) do nothing;

