ow the five features that matter most."}, {"id": "M3", "text": "Train the same model on a random 80/20 split of the test window and compare its AUC with your time-based number. Explain why the time-based number is the one you report, even if the two come out close."}, {"id": "S8", "text": "**Your segment, Google Ads acquired:** population, churners, churn rate and involuntary share in the test window, and the monthly revenue those churners took with them."}]}, {"key": "dash1", "title": "Phase 3a, Dashboard Page 1: Subscriber and Call List", "tasks": [{"id": "D3", "text": "Add a call list: the 600 highest scored subscribers in the test window, with monthly revenue and the reason to call."}, {"id": "D2", "text": "Show the top reasons behind that score (SHAP values, or the features with the biggest effect)."}, {"id": "D4", "text": "Add filters for plan, cycle, payment method, language and tier that also drive the call list."}, {"id": "D1", "text": "Build a subscriber lookup: type a Customer_ID and see the profile, the monthly usage line, bills and tickets on one timeline, and the model's churn score at the test cutoff."}, {"id": "D5", "text": "Mark involuntary risk separately: subscribers whose last renewal failed at least once."}]}, {"key": "dash2", "title": "Phase 3b, Dashboard Page 2: Model and Money", "tasks": [{"id": "D13", "text": "A segment page for Google Ads acquired."}, {"id": "D12", "text": "Feature importance for the final model, with leaky features shown greyed out as excluded."}, {"id": "D14", "text": "A threshold slider that updates precision, recall, calls made and rupees gained."}, {"id": "D7", "text": "A calibration chart: predicted against actual churn by score decile."}, {"id": "D15", "text": "Make every panel respect the segment filters."}, {"id": "D6", "text": "Model page header: AUC, PR AUC, base rate and the lift in the top 10% on the test window."}, {"id": "D10", "text": "The fade: average hours in the months before churn against stayers."}, {"id": "D11", "text": "Voluntary against involuntary churn by month and payment method."}, {"id": "D8", "text": "A profit curve: rupees gained for every call list size from 0 to the whole population, using your offer cost and success rate, with your capacity marked."}, {"id": "D9", "text": "Churn rate by cycle, plan, payment method, language and tier, all in one view."}]}, {"key": "documentation", "title": "Phase 4, Documentation", "tasks": [{"id": "DOC1", "text": "Write a model card plus a business memo. The model card covers data, population, label, leakage you removed, features, validation and test results. The memo, for the head of growth, says how many people to call, who, and what it is worth in rupees with an offer of ₹49 saving 25% of churners, and what to do about involuntary churn, which a phone call will not fix."}]}, {"key": "stretch", "title": "Stretch ideas (optional)", "tasks": [{"id": "X-S5", "text": "Which features would you add if you could log one more thing in the app? Justify with the data."}, {"id": "X-S4", "text": "Survival analysis: Kaplan-Meier curves by billing cycle and channel."}, {"id": "X-S3", "text": "Is the FIRST99 promo worth it? Compare 12 month revenue per subscriber with and without it."}]}], "brief": "**Your business brief (shared with 4 other buyers):** segment **Google Ads acquired**, offer cost **₹49**, save rate **25%**, call capacity **600**."}$pack$::jsonb
